10:T42b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/#organization","name":"M1sch1ef Managed","url":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/"},{"@type":"WebPage","url":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001","name":"The Hollow Hoard — Edition 1: The Key That Bit Back","description":"An appraiser, a former ranger, and a recovery job that refuses to stay an object.","inLanguage":"en","isAccessibleForFree":true,"publisher":{"@id":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/#organization"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"M1sch1ef Comics","item":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/comics"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"The Hollow Hoard","item":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/comics/the-hollow-hoard"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"The Hollow Hoard — Edition 1: The Key That Bit Back","item":"https://m1sch1efmanaged.com/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001"}]}]}1:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$10"}}],["$","$L11","the-hollow-hoard/issue-001",{"seriesSlug":"the-hollow-hoard","seriesTitle":"The Hollow Hoard","issue":{"slug":"issue-001","number":1,"title":"The Key That Bit Back","nextTitle":"The Borrowed Flame","summary":"An appraiser, a former ranger, and a recovery job that refuses to stay an object.","publishedAt":"2026-10-29T01:13:02.547Z","storyPages":12,"cover":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/00-cover.webp","pages":[{"number":0,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/00-cover.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"1081ed2971e5f5c88bea4acf8ec9243ae3f2df650d6afc2ecb4e4c7d830404f2","description":"Ren Calder, Tamsin and the small copper creature Latch on the cover of The Key That Bit Back.","dialogue":[]},{"number":1,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/01.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"c4b3fc0904ce17d65d71d6e715285cae24c8c0178baa50ebd9b1564e4910fc8b","description":"At a harbor stall, Ren honestly appraises Pella’s brass valve. Tamsin arrives with a work notice.","dialogue":["CAPTION: SILTMARKET. WEST QUAY.","PELLA: I was told this controlled the sea.","REN: It controls a kiln vent, Pella.","SIGN: RELIC APPRAISALS","REN: Modern teeth. Old brass, not ancient magic.","PELLA: So it's worthless.","REN: Still useful. I'll fit it at your kiln.","PELLA: For what I can pay?","REN: For what the work is worth.","TAMSIN: Ren Calder. Is this how you pay the rent?","REN: Good afternoon to you too, Tamsin."]},{"number":2,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/02.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"d51dd1dfef00a4e29045d2825cd78f70cad0d58d84bf88cc6e388412fe8db009","description":"Tamsin’s guild pass has been refused. With rent due and few coins left, she and Ren consider a recovery job.","dialogue":["TAMSIN: They refused my pass again.","REN: Does the harbor guild miss its best ranger?","TAMSIN: Former ranger. I gave the badge back.","REN: They've got a long memory.","TAMSIN: Three weeks' rent. The loftkeeper wants it by dawn.","REN: My last client wants a second opinion instead of paying.","TAMSIN: One recovery. Enough to clear it.","REN: What's the catch?"]},{"number":3,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/03.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"ad95e0c30af01ff29908f5234040e918c794e74192e51d2ced9bb018614ed67d","description":"The pair accept the job and enter coastal ruins. Tamsin checks the tide; Ren carries their last heatstone.","dialogue":["TAMSIN: One brass key. West breakwater vault. Return intact.","REN: Anonymous buyer. Generous fee.","TAMSIN: The tide gives us minutes. That's the fee.","REN: I identify it. You get us out.","TAMSIN: And you follow my lead.","REN: Last heatstone. Half a charge.","TAMSIN: Keep some for tonight.","REN: A key, rent, and a bed.","TAMSIN: Key first. Bed later."]},{"number":4,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/04.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"b75ab36320fff4a5d2cfc8ded32f2ad88580c0ae6cc075576631dd839d6f6241","description":"Inside the vault, the apparent brass key uncurls into a shivering creature chained to a stone warden.","dialogue":["CAPTION: LOW TIDE. FIVE MINUTES LEFT.","TAMSIN: One brass key. One month's rent.","REN: I like the sound of rent.","TAMSIN: Don't touch the black iron.","REN: Since when do keys need chains?","SFX: TIK","REN: Tamsin... keys don't shiver."]},{"number":5,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/05.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"dd9881cad408bf451680bc0843c2949253ee1b070d41df70fbf60c908db04052","description":"Ren tries the clamp. The warden wakes, strikes the pedestal and triggers the closing exit.","dialogue":["TAMSIN: It's feeding that thing.","REN: It's barely breathing.","REN: Easy. I've got you.","SFX: KLIK","SFX: KRRROM","TAMSIN: Down!","REN: That wasn't a keyhole.","TAMSIN: I noticed."]},{"number":6,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/06.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"da8d0582d9580272c93a4467b459116d4de289593f40718b154f588d6b7e76ab","description":"As Tamsin holds the warden off, Ren realizes the creature needs heat and chooses to give up their last heatstone.","dialogue":["TAMSIN: The door's closing!","REN: You don't want gold.","REN: You want heat.","TAMSIN: That's our last heatstone.","TAMSIN: It won't recharge.","REN: I'd rather lose the stone."]},{"number":7,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/07.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"3f5cf680ee9127eb293208ea7cb0d774d96f3dea077b2039ff5703e3eee7e65b","description":"The creature absorbs the heat, bites through its clamp and stops the warden. Tamsin pulls Ren toward the exit.","dialogue":["REN: Take it.","SFX: FSSSH","SFX: KRAK","TAMSIN: Now!"]},{"number":8,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/08.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"7b62bac1fe4543f80b1de5755277adf32b84df3e2f0cc4e5c8b9311d7ebddbc0","description":"Tamsin sacrifices her spear to hold the door. Both escape with the creature, which they name Latch.","dialogue":["SFX: GRRNNK","REN: Your spear!","TAMSIN: Keep moving.","SFX: WHOOOSH","TAMSIN: No key. No heatstone. No spear.","REN: Everyone breathing, though.","TAMSIN: What's it called?","REN: Latch.","TAMSIN: Of course it is."]},{"number":9,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/09.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"845d1a29143aa370e3130e3b3f79d62f93d6ce2b35cc832ce2f7f9019b8b6123","description":"Ren apologizes for endangering Tamsin. They agree that next time they will choose together.","dialogue":["REN: Your wrist?","TAMSIN: Bruised. The spear took the worst.","REN: I'll buy you another.","TAMSIN: That one took six months.","TAMSIN: You touched the clamp after I warned you.","REN: I saw it suffering. I stopped looking at the room.","REN: I put you in danger. I'm sorry.","TAMSIN: Next time, we choose together."]},{"number":10,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/10.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"f065c17a8411218e905094966ca2c75235c725683525c295ead42d13e41c8609","description":"At the Recovery House, the clerk offers their rent in exchange for Latch. Together they cancel the job instead.","dialogue":["REN: Your key was alive. Someone wired it into a warden.","CLERK: The order is for an intact delivery.","TAMSIN: We nearly died recovering it.","CLERK: No delivery, no payment.","CLERK: Leave it here. You'll have your rent.","REN: And what happens to it?","CLERK: The buyer's business.","TAMSIN: Then cancel the job.","REN: Both our names."]},{"number":11,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/11.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"d9d914628caa16221e40496f865d4b8dd0751a19c457d3954b7e732b9b12090a","description":"The pair shelter Latch beside a bathhouse pipe and plan to find Pella. Tamsin notices a mark on the broken clamp.","dialogue":["REN: The bathhouse vent. It's warm.","TAMSIN: Until the night valve shuts.","REN: Pella's kiln, then?","TAMSIN: She'll want more than a sad story.","REN: I still owe her a valve fitting.","REN: You don't have to stay.","TAMSIN: You owe me a spear. I'm keeping you alive to pay for it.","REN: At least we can sell the iron.","TAMSIN: Wait. Let me see that mark."]},{"number":12,"src":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/images/12.webp","width":1024,"height":1536,"sha256":"7c45d521bf43c658ea12d939b97f0208d5c25551169569460817ffd613f5ec98","description":"The clamp bears the buyer’s mark and number nine. Across the harbor, Curator Vey orders the living specimen returned.","dialogue":["TAMSIN: The buyer's mark. On its chain.","REN: He knew it was alive.","TAMSIN: Number nine.","TAMSIN: How many others are there?","REN: First, we keep this one alive.","CAPTION: CURATOR VEY.","CURATOR VEY: Bring back the specimen, alive.","CAPTION: NEXT: THE BORROWED FLAME."]}],"pdf":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-001/The-Hollow-Hoard-01.pdf","pdfSha256":"e2649a25e6870cf75d52c5a483999ea712f7dff3d8dcfcc03cecad3d92c44d82","pdfBytes":18518977},"nextIssue":{"title":"The Borrowed Flame","href":"/comics/the-hollow-hoard/issue-002"},"nextReleaseAt":null,"seasonEnd":false}]]
